<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Diyarbakir</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Diyarbakir, the ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amida">Amida</a>, is a city in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> on the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tigris">Tigris</a>. It was a key fortress on the frontier between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a>, captured by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shapur-ii">Shapur II</a> in 359 CE after a siege. Much later the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safavid-empire">Safavid Empire</a> lost it to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-chaldiran">Battle of Chaldiran</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/diyarbakir.jpg" alt="Diyarbakir" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cemallamec · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Goletli_Park,_Diyarbakir.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
